1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,640
What do we know about human presence inside the Grata del Boe marino?

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:08,560
The cave is not only a place of extraordinary natural beauty,

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:12,240
it is also a site of great archaeological interest.

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:18,400
The evidence gathered indicates that the cave was frequented as far back as prehistoric times.

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:24,240
Looking at the wall in front of you, you can see a panel of particularly significant rock carvings,

6
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,520
approximately 20 anthropomorphic figures,

7
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:33,200
incised by hammering, a coupule, a small circular hollow carved into the rock,

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,360
and two concentric circles with a further coupule at the center.

9
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:42,320
According to scholars, these carvings may date back to the Ozeary culture,

10
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:47,920
4,000 to 3,500 BC, or the filigosa culture,

11
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:55,840
3,000 to 2,500 BC, certainly at a time when the sea level was several meters lower than today,

12
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,520
and access to the cave most likely took place from the land.

13
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:05,440
If you look towards the lower right, you will notice an isolated figure with a distinctive

14
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:12,320
candelabra structure equipped with multiple limbs. Just above it, two figures can be made out

15
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:18,000
with oblique lateral appendages. Higher still, there is a figure with arms and legs

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,240
bent in the same direction. All the figures display elongated, curved, and inclined limbs

17
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:30,400
arranged irregularly around the concentric motifs. The most widely accepted interpretation

18
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:36,000
suggests that the scene depicts a group of praying figures arranged around a circular symbol,

19
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,280
perhaps connected to religious rituals or to symbolic practices related to nature.

20
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:48,880
Similar stylized anthropomorphic representations can also be found at other Italian sites,

21
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:55,200
such as the Nakuen National Rock Carving Park, the Sasconka site, and the Grotta del Papa.

22
00:01:55,920 --> 00:02:00,880
The similarities between places that are geographically very distant from one another

23
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:07,520
suggest the existence in ancient times of a shared cultural network in which symbols and

24
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:14,880
ritual practices spread among different communities. What you are looking at is not merely carvings

25
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:21,680
in rock, you are looking at a testimony to the prehistoric spirituality of Sardinia. At this precise

26
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:32,560
spot, nature and human presence meet, leaving a mark that spans thousands of years of history.

